; pi4NeonBox.pi4 - Neon_Box ON THE HDMI SCREEN, THROUGH V3D, WITH THE
; ALPHA BLEND IN THE TILE BUFFER. Counted pixels, not a photograph.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THIS IS FOR
; ======================================================================
;  pi4V3dTri.pi4 rasterised a triangle into a 64 x 64 buffer in DRAM -
;  ONE TILE, and memory nothing scans out. Four things stand between
;  that and the NeonArcade engine drawing on a monitor, and this
;  program is the first run that has all four in it at once:
;
;    1. MULTI-TILE. 1920 x 1080 is 30 x 17 = 510 tiles. Every piece of
;       tile arithmetic in v3d.pi4 - the supertile sizing, the
;       supertile sweep, the tile allocation pool, the tile state
;       buffer, the partial tiles at the right and bottom edges -
;       collapses to the identity at 64 x 64 and NOTHING HAS EVER
;       EXERCISED IT.
;
;    2. A V3D PAGE TABLE THAT REACHES THE FRAMEBUFFER. Every address
;       the CLE, the PTB and the TLB touch is virtual
;       (v3d_submit.c:1054-1055) and the firmware puts the surface at
;       $3E2CB000 on this board, so the table is about a megabyte
;       rather than the sixteen kilobytes every probe so far has used.
;
;    3. MORE THAN ONE DRAW CALL IN A LIST. The triangle was one.
;
;    4. THE BLEND. This is the one that justifies the whole exercise:
;       the A72 needs 2172.0 ms for a full-surface alpha blend against
;       a 25 ms budget (pi4NeonLiar.pi4:256-262).
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE PASS CRITERION IS COUNTED PIXELS. ALL 2,073,600 OF THEM.
; ======================================================================
;  The surface is poisoned from the CPU, the GPU draws, and then EVERY
;  PIXEL is read back and compared against the value this program
;  computed for that pixel on the CPU. Pixels are grouped BY TILE as
;  well as by region, so the answer is not only "how many were right"
;  but "how many of the 510 tiles were completely right, and which was
;  the first that was not" - which is what makes this a multi-tile
;  test rather than a big single-tile test.
;
;  THE COLOURS ARE MULTI-BYTE ON PURPOSE, all four bytes distinct in
;  every one of them, so a channel swap, a byte-order fault or a
;  16-bit store cannot pass unnoticed:
;
;    clear      R $10  G $20  B $30  A $FF
;    box A      R $40  G $80  B $C0  A $FF      opaque
;    box B      R $E0  G $50  B $90  A $80      half transparent
;    box C      R $22  G $CC  B $66  A $FF      opaque, scissored
;
;  AND THE PROGRAM PRINTS THE RAW WORD IT FOUND at a pixel in the
;  middle of box A before it judges anything. If the channel order is
;  the other way round, that one line says so directly rather than
;  leaving 2 million failures to be interpreted.
;
;  BOX B OVERLAPS BOX A AND THE CLEAR, which is the whole point: the
;  same source colour blended against two different destinations gives
;  two different answers, and both are computed here in integer
;  arithmetic and checked. A blend that was silently a copy would
;  match neither.
;
;  BOX C IS DRAWN 400 x 400 THROUGH A 200 x 150 SCISSOR. The pixels
;  outside the scissor and inside the box are the test: they must
;  still hold the clear colour. A scissor that did nothing would paint
;  120,000 pixels that are counted as wrong.
;
;  THE GUARD PAGE is DRAM this program owns and DELIBERATELY DOES NOT
;  MAP through the V3D MMU. A word in it that changed means an engine
;  wrote through an address this program never authorised.
;
; ======================================================================
;  RUNNING IT
; ======================================================================
;  PureMetalForge.exe --compile RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/pi4NeonBox.pi4 -t pi4 \
;      --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000 --entry-returns \
;      -o neonbox.img
;  then load neonbox.img on the board and read its serial output.
;
;  THE MONITOR IS THE SECOND WITNESS. The screen goes grey with the
;  poison, then the clear colour with three rectangles on it. Neither
;  step is evidence - the counts are - but a run that leaves grey on
;  the screen has told the room the CPU wrote and the GPU did not.

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/uart.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/timer.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/safety.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/mailbox.pi4"
; NO DMA ENGINE IN THIS BUILD, and that is deliberate. The one thing
; this program has to be able to say is WHICH ENGINE WROTE THE PIXELS,
; so the only writers here are the A72 and the V3D.
#DSP_DMA_LINKED = 0
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/display.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3d.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/neon.pi4"

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE MEMORY MAP.
;
;  The payload's low window is $00400000..$07EFFFFF; the image is at
;  $00400000 and the stack grows down from $03000000. THE MONITOR'S
;  VARIABLES ARE AT $08200000..$089FFFFF AND THE GENET RX RING IS AT
;  $08100000 - neither is in this window and neither may be touched.
;  The arena sits at $04000000, well above the stack and well below
;  both.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#NB_ARENA       = $04000000
#NB_ARENA_BYTES = $01000000        ; 16 MB

#NB_POISON = $A5A5A5A5

; The four colours, as logical RGBA. Every byte distinct within each.
#NB_CLEAR_R = $10
#NB_CLEAR_G = $20
#NB_CLEAR_B = $30
#NB_A_R = $40
#NB_A_G = $80
#NB_A_B = $C0
#NB_B_R = $E0
#NB_B_G = $50
#NB_B_B = $90
#NB_B_A = $80
#NB_C_R = $22
#NB_C_G = $CC
#NB_C_B = $66

; The geometry.
#NB_AX = 200
#NB_AY = 150
#NB_AW = 400
#NB_AH = 300

#NB_BX = 400
#NB_BY = 250
#NB_BW = 400
#NB_BH = 300

#NB_CX = 900
#NB_CY = 500
#NB_CW = 400
#NB_CH = 400
#NB_SX = 1000
#NB_SY = 600
#NB_SW = 200
#NB_SH = 150

; ======================================================================
;  OUTPUT
; ======================================================================
Procedure PutC(c.i)
  UartWrite(c)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutS(*s)
  UartWriteStr(*s)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutNl()
  PrintNl()
  UartDrain()
EndProcedure

Procedure PutHex(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  UartWrite(36)                              ; 36 is the dollar sign
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      UartWrite(48 + n)
    Else
      UartWrite(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure PutPad(*name, width.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  n = 0
  i = 0
  While PeekA(*name + i) <> 0
    n = n + 1
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  While n < width
    UartWrite(32)
    n = n + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure RowHex(*name, v.i)
  PutPad(*name, 30)
  PutHex(v, 8)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure RowDec(*name, v.i)
  PutPad(*name, 30)
  PrintDec(v)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure PutErr(e.i)
  If e = 0
    PutS("OK")
  Else
    PutS("error ")
    PrintDec(e)
  EndIf
EndProcedure

Procedure PutMs(us.i)
  Define w.i
  Define f.i
  w = us / 1000
  f = us - (w * 1000)
  PrintDec(w)
  UartWrite(46)                              ; 46 is the full stop
  UartWrite(48 + (f / 100))
  UartWrite(48 + ((f / 10) - ((f / 100) * 10)))
  UartWrite(48 + (f - ((f / 10) * 10)))
  UartWriteStr(" ms")
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE EXPECTATION, COMPUTED ON THE CPU
;
;  dst = src * a + dst * (1 - a), non-premultiplied, on every channel
;  INCLUDING alpha - which is what GL_SRC_ALPHA / GL_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA
;  through glBlendFunc means, and what Mesa lowers it to on both the
;  colour and the alpha equation (v3dx_emit.c:104-121).
;
;  In 0..255 integer arithmetic with round to nearest:
;
;      out = (src * a + dst * (255 - a) + 127) / 255
;
;  THE HARDWARE'S OWN ROUNDING IS NOT WRITTEN DOWN ANYWHERE ON THIS
;  DISK, so the test counts THREE outcomes and not two: exactly equal,
;  within one on every channel, and wrong. A pass on "within one" with
;  zero exact would be a real finding about the rounding and would be
;  reported as one rather than hidden by a tolerance.
; ======================================================================
Procedure.i BlendCh(src.i, dst.i, a.i)
  ProcedureReturn ((src * a) + (dst * (255 - a)) + 127) / 255
EndProcedure

Global expClear.i
Global expA.i
Global expBoverClear.i
Global expBoverA.i
Global expC.i

Procedure BuildExpectations()
  Define r.i
  Define g.i
  Define b.i
  Define a.i

  ; The surface word. pi4V3dFbClear.pi4 records that DisplayRGB(12,20,92)
  ; is $FF0C145C on this board, so the packed word is (A<<24)|(R<<16)|
  ; (G<<8)|B and byte 0 of memory is BLUE. That is display.pi4's BGR
  ; default order (dsp_order = #MBX_FB_ORDER_BGR).
  expClear = Neon_RGBA(#NB_CLEAR_R, #NB_CLEAR_G, #NB_CLEAR_B, 255)
  expA     = Neon_RGBA(#NB_A_R, #NB_A_G, #NB_A_B, 255)
  expC     = Neon_RGBA(#NB_C_R, #NB_C_G, #NB_C_B, 255)

  a = #NB_B_A
  r = BlendCh(#NB_B_R, #NB_CLEAR_R, a)
  g = BlendCh(#NB_B_G, #NB_CLEAR_G, a)
  b = BlendCh(#NB_B_B, #NB_CLEAR_B, a)
  expBoverClear = Neon_RGBA(r, g, b, BlendCh(a, 255, a))

  r = BlendCh(#NB_B_R, #NB_A_R, a)
  g = BlendCh(#NB_B_G, #NB_A_G, a)
  b = BlendCh(#NB_B_B, #NB_A_B, a)
  expBoverA = Neon_RGBA(r, g, b, BlendCh(a, 255, a))
EndProcedure

; What SHOULD pixel (x,y) hold? The regions are checked in painting
; order, last painted first.
Procedure.i Expected(x.i, y.i)
  ; Box C, but only where the scissor let it through.
  If x >= #NB_SX And x < (#NB_SX + #NB_SW)
    If y >= #NB_SY And y < (#NB_SY + #NB_SH)
      If x >= #NB_CX And x < (#NB_CX + #NB_CW)
        If y >= #NB_CY And y < (#NB_CY + #NB_CH)
          ProcedureReturn expC
        EndIf
      EndIf
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ; Box B, over box A or over the clear.
  If x >= #NB_BX And x < (#NB_BX + #NB_BW)
    If y >= #NB_BY And y < (#NB_BY + #NB_BH)
      If x >= #NB_AX And x < (#NB_AX + #NB_AW)
        If y >= #NB_AY And y < (#NB_AY + #NB_AH)
          ProcedureReturn expBoverA
        EndIf
      EndIf
      ProcedureReturn expBoverClear
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ; Box A.
  If x >= #NB_AX And x < (#NB_AX + #NB_AW)
    If y >= #NB_AY And y < (#NB_AY + #NB_AH)
      ProcedureReturn expA
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn expClear
EndProcedure

Procedure.i Near1(a.i, b.i)
  Define i.i
  Define d.i
  Define sa.i
  Define sb.i
  For i = 0 To 3
    sa = (a >> (i * 8)) & $FF
    sb = (b >> (i * 8)) & $FF
    d = sa - sb
    If d < 0
      d = 0 - d
    EndIf
    If d > 1
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
  Next
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  VERIFICATION
; ======================================================================
Global nExact.i = 0
Global nNear.i  = 0
Global nWrong.i = 0
Global nPoison.i = 0
Global firstBadX.i = -1
Global firstBadY.i = -1
Global firstBadGot.i = 0
Global firstBadWant.i = 0
Global tilesTotal.i = 0
Global tilesClean.i = 0
Global firstBadTile.i = -1
Global guardTouched.i = 0
Global usPoison.i = 0
Global usVerify.i = 0
Global usFrame.i = 0

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  NextBoundary - the next x at which Expected() could change value,
;  for any row.
;
;  THE INNER LOOP HAS TO BE CHEAP AND THIS IS WHY THIS EXISTS. With the
;  ARM MMU off every access - INCLUDING EVERY INSTRUCTION FETCH - is
;  Device memory, and pi4NeonLiar.pi4 measured a bare read loop at
;  998 ns a pixel on this board. Calling Expected() per pixel would put
;  two million procedure calls inside that and take the run past the
;  15 s deadman. So Expected() is called ONCE PER SEGMENT and the
;  segment runs to the next rectangle edge.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i Edge(px.i, e.i, best.i)
  If e > px
    If e < best
      ProcedureReturn e
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn best
EndProcedure

Procedure.i NextBoundary(px.i, limit.i)
  Define b.i
  b = limit
  b = Edge(px, #NB_AX, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_AX + #NB_AW, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_BX, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_BX + #NB_BW, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_CX, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_CX + #NB_CW, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_SX, b)
  b = Edge(px, #NB_SX + #NB_SW, b)
  ProcedureReturn b
EndProcedure

Procedure Verify(tw.i, th.i, tx.i, ty.i)
  Define px.i
  Define py.i
  Define v.i
  Define want.i
  Define row.i
  Define bad.i
  Define x0.i
  Define y0.i
  Define x1.i
  Define y1.i
  Define tileX.i
  Define tileY.i
  Define segEnd.i
  Define a.i

  tilesTotal = tx * ty
  tileY = 0
  While tileY < ty
    tileX = 0
    While tileX < tx
      x0 = tileX * tw
      y0 = tileY * th
      x1 = x0 + tw
      y1 = y0 + th
      If x1 > Neon_SurfaceW()
        x1 = Neon_SurfaceW()
      EndIf
      If y1 > Neon_SurfaceH()
        y1 = Neon_SurfaceH()
      EndIf
      bad = 0
      py = y0
      While py < y1
        row = Neon_SurfaceBase() + (py * Neon_SurfacePitch())
        px = x0
        While px < x1
          want = Expected(px, py)
          segEnd = NextBoundary(px, x1)
          a = row + (px * 4)
          While px < segEnd
            v = PeekN(a)
            If v = want
              nExact = nExact + 1
            Else
              bad = bad + 1
              If Near1(v, want) <> 0
                nNear = nNear + 1
              ElseIf v = #NB_POISON
                nPoison = nPoison + 1
              Else
                nWrong = nWrong + 1
              EndIf
              If firstBadX < 0
                firstBadX = px
                firstBadY = py
                firstBadGot = v
                firstBadWant = want
              EndIf
            EndIf
            a = a + 4
            px = px + 1
          Wend
        Wend
        py = py + 1
      Wend
      If bad = 0
        tilesClean = tilesClean + 1
      ElseIf firstBadTile < 0
        firstBadTile = (tileY * tx) + tileX
      EndIf
      tileX = tileX + 1
    Wend
    tileY = tileY + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure VerifyGuard()
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  i = 0
  n = 4096 / 4
  While i < n
    If PeekN(Neon_GuardAddr() + (i * 4)) <> #NB_POISON
      guardTouched = guardTouched + 1
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  MAIN
; ======================================================================
Procedure.i Body()
  Define r.i
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  Define t0.i
  Define probe.i

  PutNl()
  PutS("=== pi4NeonBox - Neon_Box on the HDMI surface, through V3D ===")
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  If TimerInit() = 0
    PutS("!! the architectural counter is not running - times read 0")
    PutNl()
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  1. THE SURFACE
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("1   the HDMI surface")
  PutNl()
  If MailboxInit() = 0
    PutS("    mailbox REFUSED")
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: NO SURFACE")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If DisplayStandardTags() = 0
    PutS("    display tags REFUSED")
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: NO SURFACE")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = DisplayInit(1920, 1080, 32)
  If r <> 1
    PutS("    DisplayInit rc ")
    PrintDec(r)
    PutS("  MailboxError ")
    PrintDec(MailboxError())
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: NO SURFACE")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("width", DisplayWidth())
  RowDec("height", DisplayHeight())
  RowDec("pitch, bytes", DisplayPitch())
  RowHex("base, ARM physical", DisplayBase())
  RowDec("allocation, bytes", DisplaySize())
  If DisplayBytesPerPixel() <> 4
    PutS("verdict: NOT 32BPP")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  2. THE ENGINE
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("2   the engine")
  PutNl()
  r = NeonArena(#NB_ARENA, #NB_ARENA_BYTES)
  If r <> #NEON_OK
    PutS("    NeonArena: ")
    PutErr(r)
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: ARENA")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = NeonSurface(DisplayBase(), DisplayWidth(), DisplayHeight(), DisplayPitch())
  If r <> #NEON_OK
    PutS("    NeonSurface: ")
    PutErr(r)
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: SURFACE")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = NeonInit()
  PutS("    NeonInit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("HUB_IDENT1", V3dIdent1())
  RowDec("page table bytes", Neon_PtBytes())
  RowDec("arena bytes needed", Neon_ArenaNeed())
  RowHex("arena top", Neon_ArenaTop())
  RowHex("guard page", Neon_GuardAddr())
  RowDec("tile width", V3dTileW())
  RowDec("tile height", V3dTileH())
  RowDec("tiles across", V3dTilesX())
  RowDec("tiles down", V3dTilesY())
  RowDec("tiles total", V3dTilesX() * V3dTilesY())
  RowDec("supertile width, tiles", V3dSupertileW())
  RowDec("supertile height, tiles", V3dSupertileH())
  RowDec("frame width, supertiles", V3dFrameStW())
  RowDec("frame height, supertiles", V3dFrameStH())
  RowDec("tile alloc needed", V3dTileAllocNeeded())
  RowDec("tile state needed", V3dTileStateNeeded())
  If r <> #NEON_OK
    RowDec("V3dError", V3dError())
    PutS("verdict: NEONINIT")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If (V3dTilesX() * V3dTilesY()) < 2
    PutS("    one tile only - this probe has nothing to prove here")
    PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: NOT MULTI-TILE")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  NeonPalette()
  NeonFontDefaults()
  BuildExpectations()
  RowHex("expected clear", expClear)
  RowHex("expected box A", expA)
  RowHex("expected B over clear", expBoverClear)
  RowHex("expected B over A", expBoverA)
  RowHex("expected box C", expC)
  RowDec("channel swap in shader", Neon_RbSwapGet())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  3. POISON. The whole surface and the guard page.
  ;
  ;     THE SCREEN GOES GREY HERE. $A5A5A5A5 is a flat mid-grey, so a
  ;     human watching the monitor sees the console vanish under grey
  ;     and then the grey replaced by the picture. Neither step is
  ;     evidence - the counts are - but a run that leaves grey on the
  ;     screen has said the CPU wrote and the GPU did not.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("3   poisoning the surface")
  PutNl()
  UartDrain()
  t0 = Micros()
  n = Neon_SurfaceH()
  i = 0
  While i < n
    DspRowFill32(Neon_SurfaceBase() + (i * Neon_SurfacePitch()), Neon_SurfaceW(), #NB_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  usPoison = Micros() - t0
  i = 0
  While i < 1024
    PokeN(Neon_GuardAddr() + (i * 4), #NB_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  PutPad("poison time", 30)
  PutMs(usPoison)
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  4. THE FRAME. Three boxes and a scissor.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("4   the frame")
  PutNl()
  UartDrain()
  t0 = Micros()

  r = NeonFrameBegin(expClear)
  If r <> #NEON_OK
    PutS("    NeonFrameBegin: ")
    PutErr(r)
    PutNl()
    RowDec("V3dError", V3dError())
    PutS("verdict: FRAMEBEGIN")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  Neon_Box(#NB_AX, #NB_AY, #NB_AW, #NB_AH, Neon_RGBA(#NB_A_R, #NB_A_G, #NB_A_B, 255))
  Neon_Box(#NB_BX, #NB_BY, #NB_BW, #NB_BH, Neon_RGBA(#NB_B_R, #NB_B_G, #NB_B_B, #NB_B_A))

  Neon_ScissorSet(#NB_SX, #NB_SY, #NB_SW, #NB_SH)
  Neon_Box(#NB_CX, #NB_CY, #NB_CW, #NB_CH, Neon_RGBA(#NB_C_R, #NB_C_G, #NB_C_B, 255))
  Neon_ScissorClear()

  RowDec("draw calls", Neon_Draws())
  RowDec("boxes", Neon_Boxes())
  RowDec("vertices", Neon_Verts())
  RowDec("bin list bytes", V3dClLen())
  UartDrain()

  r = NeonFrameEnd()
  usFrame = Micros() - t0
  PutS("    NeonFrameEnd: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  PutPad("frame time, CPU + GPU", 30)
  PutMs(usFrame)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("CLE_BFC before", V3dBinBfcBefore())
  RowHex("CLE_BFC after", V3dBinBfcAfter())
  RowHex("CLE_CT0CA", V3dBinCt0ca())
  RowHex("CLE_CT0EA", V3dBinCt0ea())
  RowHex("CLE_RFC before", V3dRenderRfcBefore())
  RowHex("CLE_RFC after", V3dRenderRfcAfter())
  RowHex("CLE_CT1CA", V3dRenderCt1ca())
  RowHex("CLE_CT1EA", V3dRenderCt1ea())
  RowHex("bin ERR_STAT", V3dBinErrStat())
  RowHex("render ERR_STAT", V3dRenderErrStat())
  RowHex("bin MMU_CTL", V3dBinMmuCtl())
  RowHex("bin MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dBinVioAddr())
  RowHex("render MMU_CTL", V3dRenderMmuCtl())
  RowHex("render MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dRenderVioAddr())
  RowDec("OOM events", V3dBinOomCount())
  RowDec("bin spins", V3dBinSpins())
  RowDec("render spins", V3dRenderSpins())
  If r <> #NEON_OK
    RowDec("Neon_Error", Neon_Error())
    RowDec("V3dError", V3dError())
    PutS("verdict: FRAMEEND")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  5. THE RAW WORD, BEFORE ANY JUDGEMENT.
  ;
  ;     One pixel from the middle of box A, printed as it is. If the
  ;     channel order came out the other way round this line says so
  ;     in one number instead of two million failures.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  probe = PeekN(Neon_SurfaceBase() + ((#NB_AY + 10) * Neon_SurfacePitch()) + ((#NB_AX + 10) * 4))
  PutS("5   the raw word at the middle of box A")
  PutNl()
  RowHex("found", probe)
  RowHex("wanted", expA)
  probe = PeekN(Neon_SurfaceBase() + (10 * Neon_SurfacePitch()) + (10 * 4))
  RowHex("clear, found at (10,10)", probe)
  RowHex("clear, wanted", expClear)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  6. EVERY PIXEL, BY TILE.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("6   counting 2073600 pixels")
  PutNl()
  UartDrain()
  t0 = Micros()
  Verify(V3dTileW(), V3dTileH(), V3dTilesX(), V3dTilesY())
  usVerify = Micros() - t0
  VerifyGuard()

  RowDec("pixels exactly right", nExact)
  RowDec("pixels within one", nNear)
  RowDec("pixels still poison", nPoison)
  RowDec("pixels some other value", nWrong)
  RowDec("tiles total", tilesTotal)
  RowDec("tiles completely right", tilesClean)
  RowDec("first bad tile", firstBadTile)
  RowDec("first bad x", firstBadX)
  RowDec("first bad y", firstBadY)
  RowHex("first bad, found", firstBadGot)
  RowHex("first bad, wanted", firstBadWant)
  RowDec("guard words touched", guardTouched)
  PutPad("verify time", 30)
  PutMs(usVerify)
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  7. THE VERDICT
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  If nPoison <> 0
    PutS("verdict: THE GPU DID NOT COVER THE SURFACE - poison left")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn nPoison
  EndIf
  If guardTouched <> 0
    PutS("verdict: GUARD TOUCHED")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If nWrong <> 0
    PutS("verdict: WRONG PIXELS")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn nWrong
  EndIf
  If nNear <> 0
    PutS("verdict: OK WITHIN ONE - the blend rounds differently from")
    PutNl()
    PutS("         this program, which is a finding and not a failure")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn nExact
  EndIf
  PutS("verdict: OK - every pixel exact, multi-tile, blended, scissored")
  PutNl()
  ProcedureReturn nExact
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE WRAPPER THAT HANDS THE GPU BACK.
;
;  Main() is a wrapper and Body() is the program, for one reason:
;  Body() has a dozen early returns and EVERY ONE of them has to put
;  the V3D MMU back before the monitor gets control again. Measured on
;  the board, 2026-08-28: a payload that left the MMU enabled with its
;  own page table killed the VideoCore firmware's mailbox service, and
;  the NEXT payload could not get a surface - MAIL1_STA $80000008,
;  full of requests nobody was consuming, cleared only by a reset.
;  See NeonShutdown() in neon.pi4 for the full note.
;
;  A cleanup that has to be repeated at a dozen returns is a cleanup
;  that will be missed at one of them.
; ======================================================================
Procedure.i Main()
  Define rc.i
  rc = Body()
  NeonShutdown()
  ProcedureReturn rc
EndProcedure
